{
  "version": "2025.10",
  "description": "Environment dimensions.\n\nEach dimension owns a distinct slice (see packages/styles/README.md — the\ndimension-ownership table):\n  - Design Language → component sizing/proportions + interaction feedback\n  - Input           → ergonomics (min touch target)\n  - Density         → proportional rhythm\n\nRadius, color, and shadow are NOT design-language concerns — they belong to\nthe semantic ramp + theme (personalization). Design language never sets radius.\n\nPrevent focus zoom in mobile Safari without inflating non-editable control\n labels. Editable recipes combine this floor with their normal type token.\n\nDensity — proportional rhythm\n\nAuto-detect coarse pointers. Without this, touch ergonomics only apply when an\n app explicitly passes `input` to UIProvider — an opt-in almost nothing does, so\n controls stay at their 24px floor on phones. Declared before the attribute\n rules below (equal specificity) so an explicit data-a63-input always wins.\n\nInput — ergonomics (touch target). Independent of design language.\n\nExplicit fine-pointer choices override coarse auto-detection (hybrid devices,\n or a user who picked \"pointer\" in the appearance panel on a touchscreen).\n\nDesign language — component sizing/proportions + interaction feedback only.\nThe base :root (control.css) is the web default; iOS overrides sizing + feel.\nNo radius, color, or touch-target here.",
  "sets": {
    "01-root": {
      "sources": [
        {
          "a63": {
            "density": {
              "scale": {
                "$type": "number",
                "$value": 1
              }
            },
            "editable": {
              "font": {
                "size": {
                  "min": {
                    "$type": "dimension",
                    "$value": {
                      "value": 0,
                      "unit": "px"
                    }
                  }
                }
              }
            },
            "control": {
              "min": {
                "size": {
                  "$root": {
                    "$type": "dimension",
                    "$value": {
                      "value": 1.5,
                      "unit": "rem"
                    },
                    "$description": "Two different numbers, deliberately separate:\n   - min-size   = RENDERED geometry floor. WCAG 2.5.8 pointer minimum (24px).\n                  Touch raises it only to 32px — the smallest rendered control\n                  observed in shipping iOS apps (measured 30.6–31.5pt across two\n                  apps). Apple's Accessibility page publishes an iOS\nminimum control size* of 28x28pt, so a 32pt rendered floor\n                  sits above the documented minimum and below the 44pt default.\n                  https://developer.apple.com/design/human-interface-guidelines/accessibility\n   - min-target = INTERACTION floor. Touch raises it to 44px per Apple HIG.\n   Recipes must floor their height ramp with min-size and expand the touch\n   region with min-target. Flooring rendered height with min-target is what\n   collapses the xs/sm/md ramp to a single 44px rung on every phone.\n   See docs/design-system/web-ios-token-parity.md."
                  },
                  "lg": {
                    "$type": "dimension",
                    "$value": "{a63.control.min.size}"
                  },
                  "xl": {
                    "$type": "dimension",
                    "$value": "{a63.control.min.size}"
                  }
                },
                "target": {
                  "$root": {
                    "$type": "dimension",
                    "$value": {
                      "value": 1.5,
                      "unit": "rem"
                    }
                  },
                  "lg": {
                    "$type": "dimension",
                    "$value": "{a63.control.min.target}"
                  }
                }
              }
            },
            "row": {
              "min": {
                "size": {
                  "$type": "dimension",
                  "$value": "{a63.control.min.size}",
                  "$description": "Rendered floor for a full-width ROW (a list/panel row whose whole width is\n   the target), as opposed to a compact control sitting inside one. A row\n   cannot borrow the pseudo-element trick: rows live in clipping containers\n   (rounded panels, scroll areas) that cut an overhanging pseudo off, so the\n   row's own height has to BE the target. 44px on touch — Apple's HIG default,\n   and our own measurement of shipping iOS apps put primary rows and\n   full-width controls at 42.4-44.1pt (docs/design-system/web-ios-token-parity.md).\n   Equal to min-size on fine pointers, so desktop is unchanged."
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      ],
      "$extensions": {
        "io.atom63.css": {
          "selector": ":root"
        }
      }
    },
    "03-media-max-width-40rem-root": {
      "sources": [
        {
          "a63": {
            "editable": {
              "font": {
                "size": {
                  "min": {
                    "$type": "dimension",
                    "$value": {
                      "value": 1,
                      "unit": "rem"
                    }
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      ],
      "$extensions": {
        "io.atom63.css": {
          "selector": ":root",
          "atRule": "@media (max-width: 40rem)"
        }
      }
    },
    "04-is-data-a63-density-compact-data-density-compact": {
      "sources": [
        {
          "a63": {
            "density": {
              "scale": {
                "$type": "number",
                "$value": 0.9
              }
            },
            "space": {
              "unit": {
                "$type": "dimension",
                "$value": "{spacing.1}",
                "$extensions": {
                  "io.atom63.derive": "calc({spacing.1} * 0.875)"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      ],
      "$extensions": {
        "io.atom63.css": {
          "selector": ":is([data-a63-density='compact'], [data-density='compact'])"
        }
      }
    },
    "05-is-data-a63-density-comfortable-data-density-com": {
      "sources": [
        {
          "a63": {
            "density": {
              "scale": {
                "$type": "number",
                "$value": 1
              }
            },
            "space": {
              "unit": {
                "$type": "dimension",
                "$value": "{spacing.1}"
              }
            }
          }
        }
      ],
      "$extensions": {
        "io.atom63.css": {
          "selector": ":is([data-a63-density='comfortable'], [data-density='comfortable'])"
        }
      }
    },
    "06-media-pointer-coarse-root": {
      "sources": [
        {
          "a63": {
            "control": {
              "min": {
                "size": {
                  "$root": {
                    "$type": "dimension",
                    "$value": {
                      "value": 2,
                      "unit": "rem"
                    }
                  },
                  "lg": {
                    "$type": "dimension",
                    "$value": "{a63.control.min.size}"
                  },
                  "xl": {
                    "$type": "dimension",
                    "$value": "{a63.control.min.size}"
                  }
                },
                "target": {
                  "$root": {
                    "$type": "dimension",
                    "$value": {
                      "value": 2.75,
                      "unit": "rem"
                    }
                  },
                  "lg": {
                    "$type": "dimension",
                    "$value": {
                      "value": 3,
                      "unit": "rem"
                    }
                  },
                  "xl": {
                    "$type": "dimension",
                    "$value": {
                      "value": 3.25,
                      "unit": "rem"
                    }
                  }
                }
              }
            },
            "row": {
              "min": {
                "size": {
                  "$type": "dimension",
                  "$value": {
                    "value": 2.75,
                    "unit": "rem"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      ],
      "$extensions": {
        "io.atom63.css": {
          "selector": ":root",
          "atRule": "@media (pointer: coarse)"
        }
      }
    },
